> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based on the documentation provided, here is a structured summary and technical breakdown of the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection.

### **Overview**
This is a specialized patch set for [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) designed to maximize performance on **AMD RDNA3, RDNA3.5, and RDNA4** GPUs. It consists of **16 self-contained patches** (blocks 00–15) that can be applied individually or as a whole using `git am`.

*   **Base Commit:** `790cf51aa` (Re-based on 2026-09-13).
*   **Target Architectures:**
    *   **RDNA 3:** `gfx1100` (RX 7900 XTX/XT, RX 7800 XT)
    *   **RDNA 3.5:** `gfx1150`/`gfx1151` (Strix Point / Strix Halo APUs)
    *   **RDNA 4:** `gfx1200`/`gfx1201` (RX 9060 XT, RX 9070/9070 XT)
*   **Key Benefit:** RDNA4 sees the most improvement, but significant optimizations are back-ported to RDNA3/3.5.

---

### **The 16 Patches (Blocks)**

| Block | Description | Key Features / Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **0000** | **Structural & Arch Fixes** | Base patch. Fixes FA small-batch KV-split width invariance and Vulkan masked-V/freed-cell issues. |
| **0001** | **Adaptive MTP** | Adds `--draft-mtp-adaptive` for dynamic draft depth. |
| **0002** | **Chunked GDN Prefill** | Fused chunked gated-delta-net prefill kernel (bf16/WMMA). Arch-segregated kernels for gfx12 and gfx11. |
| **0003** | **BF16 KV Cache** | Native BF16 KV cache + native-BF16 flash-attn. Includes HIP masked-V/freed-cell fixes. |
| **0004** | **WMMA Flash-Attn** | RDNA4 WMMA flash-attn + Q6_K mmq prefill perf. **Note:** Also runs on RDNA3.0/3.5 with tuned head limits (576 for RDNA3.0, 320 for RDNA3.5). |
| **0005** | **CPU Bit-Identical** | Ensures CPU decode/verify batches are bit-identical. |
| **0006** | **Host-Buffer Revert** | Reverts host-buffer changes for discrete GPUs (functional delta dropped in 2026-09-08 re-base; now only carries rationale comments). |
| **0007** | **Meta Device Skip** | Skips meta device-wrapper. |
| **0008** | **Fused-Core Prefill** | Fused-core prefill kernels + GPU bit-identical results. **Requires blocks 03+04.** Amended with `mul_mat+add` shape guard and quantized KV-type enablement (`q4_1`/`q5_0`/`q5_1`). |
| **0009** | **Meta-Buffer Headroom** | Adds compute-container headroom for meta-buffers. |
| **0010** | **K-Quant Boosts** | Optimizes Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 mmvq VDR. Adds dedicated RDNA3.5 mmvq table. **Warning:** Changes decode numerics (reorders fp32 reduction). |
| **0011** | **Skip CUDA Graphs (Prefill)** | Skips CUDA graphs for multi-token prefill; keeps them for decode. |
| **0012** | **Hybrid HIP All-Reduce** | Custom internal all-reduce for small-tensor decode. **RDNA4-only** (gfx1200/gfx1201). Falls back to RCCL elsewhere. |
| **0013** | **Fused MoE MMQ** | Fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + mmvq short-K item-split. Supports RDNA4, RDNA3.5, and RDNA3.0. Includes fixes for MTP regressions and band-uniformity. |
| **0014** | **Qwen4exp Support** | Support for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (qwen4exp). Includes QSA sparse FA, fused indexer top-k, HC_MIX/HC_COMBINE ops, and MTP draft-head. |
| **0015** | **Attention-Memory Wins** | Frees VRAM via derived kq mask, native q8_0/bf16 K/V in FA, QSA score-chain memory, and ggml-alloc unused-view release. Saves ~3.4 GiB/GPU on qwen4exp. |

---

### **Key Technical Highlights**

1.  **Runtime Arch Selection:**
    *   No compile-time arch gating. A single binary built with `GPU_TARGETS="gfx1100;gfx1151;gfx1201"` will automatically select the correct kernel path at runtime based on the detected GPU.
    *   **Exception:** Block 12 (Hybrid All-Reduce) is strictly gated to RDNA4.

2.  **Greedy Purity & Numerics:**
    *   **Block 10 (K-Quant Boosts)** is the **only** patch that changes decode numerics on *any* architecture due to reordered fp32 reductions in VDR kernels.
    *   **Block 13 (Fused MoE)** also affects numerics on specific rows (short-K, ncols==1) but was fixed to restore bit-identity for `W=1..8` in recent amendments.
    *   If 100% greedy purity across builds is required, **exclude Block 10**.

3.  **VRAM Savings (Block 15):**
    *   **Qwen4exp:** ~3.4 GiB/GPU + ~1.2 GiB host saved.
    *   **Dense Models:** ~800 MiB/GPU + ~800 MiB host saved.
    *   Performance cost is minimal (~1.3% prefill, ~0.3% decode).

4.  **Qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) Support (Block 14):**
    *   Includes QSA (Query-Sparse Attention) sparse FA, fused indexer top-k, and specific decode/prefill fusions.
    *   Recent fixes ensure `plain decode == draft-mtp verify` for `n_max <= 7`.

---

### **Installation & Usage**

*   **Do NOT use `git apply`** on concatenated patches. It silently drops hunks.
*   **Use `git am`** or the provided script:
    ```bash
    scripts/apply-all.sh
    ```
*   **Manual Application:**
    ```bash
    git am patches/0000-*.patch
    git am patches/0001-*.patch
    # ... up to 0015
    ```
*   **Build:**
    ```bash
    cmake -B build -DGGML_HIP=ON -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-march=native"
    cmake --build build --config Release
    ```
    *   For multi-arch support: `GPU_TARGETS="gfx1100;gfx1151;gfx1201"`

---

### **Recent Changes (2026-09-13 Re-base)**

*   **Re-based** onto llama.cpp master `790cf51aa` (70 commits ahead of previous base).
*   **Resolved 4 upstream clashes:**
    1.  `gfx1201` FA tuning.
    2.  `GGML_FA_QUANTS` handling.
    3.  MoE MMQ `ncols_opt`.
    4.  Indexer V cache.
*   **Validation:**
    *   `test-backend-ops`: 18061/18061 passed.
    *   4B/27B width probes and 27B 8-type text gate are pure and byte-identical to previous delivery.
    *   Qwen4exp 3-GPU MTP is pure and byte-identical.
    *   Benchmarks show performance equal to or ahead of stock `9113cc188`.

---

### **Important Caveats**

1.  **Block 12 (All-Reduce):** Only works on RDNA4. On RDNA3/3.5, it falls back to RCCL.
2.  **Block 10 (K-Quant):** Changes decode numerics. Exclude if strict bit-identical output across different builds is required.
3.  **Block 13 (MoE):** Recent fixes ensure bit-identity for `W=1..8` on RDNA3.5 and RDNA3.0, but verify your specific model configuration.
4.  **Upstreaming:** Some blocks (e.g., Block 12) are candidates for upstream contribution but are currently fork-local due to arch-specific gating.

